<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="698c6">&lt;p&gt;
    The cutover runbook documents transition activities for each of the business and technology domains and describes the
    transition window in which the activities will be executed. It presents the next lower level of detail that is outlined
    in the cutover and deployment approach and detailed further in the cutover and deployment plan.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The runbook assigns tasks, timing and scheduling details for the steps and efforts of the transition cutover, including
    scheduling and timing of procedures to discontinue production usage of the legacy system, to specific individuals. A
    key benefit of this documented process is to describe the final deployment efforts to provide a smooth transition to
    production and eventual adoption into normal operations.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The majority of the runbook consists of the instruction set for the cutover. In addition, the runbook reviews readiness
    criteria and provides the basis for approval to proceed to the go / no-go checklist.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A blackout period (specific time frame when production systems and services will be unavailable and/or live production
    data is cached until services are back online) may be required to resolve minor last minute deployment issues not
    warranting a no-go decision. A blackout period can also be scheduled to complete the deployment. The length of the
    blackout period will vary and should consider operations in other locations and time zones and be mindful of applicable
    downstream processes.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
